Description\r\n\r\nJust helping any internet searchers coming around until Webpack fixes this.\r\n\r\nIf you are \r\n\r\n - using Webpack 3\r\n - with parser.amd = false as per the [Readme](https://github.com/swagger-api/swagger-codegen/blob/master/samples/client/petstore/javascript/README.md)\r\n\r\nYou will run into this issue https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5198.\r\n\r\nThe problematic line for me is in ApiClient.prototype.isFileParam.\r\n\r\n```javascript\r\n    if (typeof window === 'undefined' &&\r\n        typeof require === 'function' && // <------ here\r\n        require('fs') &&\r\n        param instanceof require('fs').ReadStream) {\r\n      return true;\r\n    }\r\n```\r\n\r\n##### Swagger-codegen version\r\n\r\nTried with 2.2.0 and 2.2.2.\r\n\r\n##### Swagger declaration file content or url\r\n\r\n##### Command line used for generation\r\n\r\n##### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n - `require()` Swagger generated files from Webpack 3.\r\n\r\n##### Related issues\r\n\r\n##### Suggest a Fix\r\n\r\nGo back to the old hack using `imports-loader?define=false` which still works until the bug is fixed.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/swagger-api/swagger-codegen/issues/5975/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/swagger-api/swagger-codegen/issues/5975/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/312785800","html_url":"https://github.com/webpack/webpack/issues/5198#issuecomment-312785800","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/5198","id":312785800,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxMjc4NTgwMA==","user":{"login":"darylteo","id":1226920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjY5MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1226920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo","html_url":"https://github.com/darylteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2017-07-04T05:46:09Z","updated_at":"2017-07-04T05:46:09Z","body":"For google searchers: if you're using Swagger-Codegen, and have set \"parser: { amd: false }\" in your rules, this bug will break your build. Revert back to the old \"imports-loader?define=>false\" hack  to workaround.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure why this works, other than perhaps \"imports-loader\" is doing something else to it.\r\n\r\nHopefully this helps to narrow down issue. I'm guessing there is a regression in the commonjs transpiler or something, but I'm not familiar enough with the codebase to figure it out. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/webpack/webpack/issues/comments/312785800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"darylteo","id":1226920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMjY5MjA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1226920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo","html_url":"https://github.com/darylteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darylteo/following{/other_u